.TH LLM-LOADTEST 1 "2026-10-26" "llm-loadtest" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llm-loadtest \- load-test OpenAI-compatible streaming LLM endpoints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llm-loadtest run
.B \-\-base\-url
.I URL
.B \-\-model
.I NAME
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B llm-loadtest mock
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B llm-loadtest compare
.RB [ \-\-threshold
.IR PCT ]
.I BASE.json HEAD.json
.br
.B llm-loadtest version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B llm-loadtest
sends streaming chat-completion requests to an OpenAI-compatible server
(vLLM, SGLang, llama.cpp, Ollama, OpenAI and others) and reports time to
first token, inter-token latency, time per output token, end-to-end latency
and throughput, with p50, p90, p95 and p99 for each load level.
.PP
Load is either closed-loop, at a fixed number of requests in flight, or
open-loop, at a target arrival rate. Open-loop latency is measured from each
request's scheduled start, so a server that falls behind cannot hide the
queueing it causes.
.PP
Run
.B llm-loadtest
.I command
.B \-h
for the full list of flags of a command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run a load test and print a Markdown report. The main flags are
.B \-\-concurrency
(a level, or a list such as 1,2,4,8 for a sweep),
.B \-\-rate
(open-loop arrivals in requests per second, also as a list),
.B \-\-duration
or
.B \-\-requests
per stage,
.B \-\-input\-tokens
or
.B \-\-dataset
for prompts,
.B \-\-max\-tokens
and
.B \-\-out
(a .json, .csv or .md file; repeatable).
.TP
.B mock
Serve an OpenAI-compatible chat-completions API with synthetic latency on
.B \-\-addr
(default 127.0.0.1:8000), for rehearsing a benchmark without a GPU.
.B \-\-slots
limits concurrent generations;
.BR \-\-ttft ,
.B \-\-itl
and
.B \-\-output\-tokens
take distributions such as normal:150ms,30ms or uniform:64,256.
.TP
.B compare
Compare two JSON results stage by stage. With
.BR \-\-threshold ,
exit with status 1 when a throughput or latency metric is more than
.I PCT
percent worse.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, the Go version and the platform.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Sent as a bearer token, but only when
.B \-\-base\-url
points at api.openai.com.
.B \-\-api\-key\-env
.I NAME
reads the key from another variable and sends it to
.BR \-\-base\-url .
The key is never printed or saved.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The run failed, or
.B compare
found a regression.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid flags or arguments.
.TP
.B 130
Stopped by SIGINT or SIGTERM; partial results were written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Rehearse against the built-in mock:
.PP
.nf
.RS
llm-loadtest mock \-\-slots 8 &
llm-loadtest run \-\-base\-url http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1 \-\-model mock \e
    \-\-max\-tokens 64 \-\-concurrency 1,4,16 \-\-duration 10s
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/aozmekik/llm-loadtest
